---
import ProseLayout from '../../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { apps } from '../../config/apps';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  updated={site.legalUpdated}
  description="How ChrisGonzalez.net handles information. No analytics, no tracking, no third-party requests."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy', href: '/legal/privacy/' }]}
>
  <p>
    This policy covers the website <strong>chrisgonzalez.net</strong>, run by Chris Gonzalez, an independent software developer
    (“I”, “me”). Each app has its own privacy policy:
  </p>
  <ul>
    {apps.map((a) => <li><a href={`/apps/${a.slug}/privacy/`}>{a.name} privacy policy</a></li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use analytics, advertising, tracking pixels, social media embeds or third-party fonts. It does not
    ask for your name, email or anything else, and it doesn’t set any cookies unless you change the colour theme.
  </p>

  <h2>Information this website handles</h2>
  <h3>Server logs</h3>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub receives technical information when you visit — such as your IP
    address, browser and the page requested — to deliver and secure the site. I don’t have access to these logs. GitHub’s handling
    of this data is described in the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>
  <h3>Your theme preference</h3>
  <p>
    If you switch between the dark and light theme, your choice is stored in a cookie on your device so the site remembers it. See
    the <a href="/legal/cookies/">cookie policy</a> for details and to clear it.
  </p>
  <h3>Email</h3>
  <p>
    If you email me, I receive your email address and whatever you choose to include. I use it only to reply and to help you, keep
    it no longer than needed, and never share it or add you to a mailing list.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to app stores, GitHub and other sites take you to services with their own privacy policies. Store pages are run by Apple,
    Google or Microsoft, not by me.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live — including under the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation — you have rights to access,
    correct and delete personal data about you, and to object to its use. Because this website doesn’t collect personal data, the
    only data I may hold is our email correspondence. To access or delete it, email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}?subject=Privacy%20request`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. You also have the right to complain
    to your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes — for example, if privacy-friendly analytics are added — this page will be updated first, and the date above will change.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Chris Gonzalez · <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a></p>
</ProseLayout>
